<div class="togglecontainer av-m8fal8da-2cafb2dfa5dd4a2ccc54f36b4b8ca464 av-elegant-toggle avia-builder-el-34 el_after_av_heading avia-builder-el-last toggle_close_all enable_toggles" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8fagqmc-292dfe6ffe1d5c98765880f8d0c7194c" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: What is EmSella Therapy, and how does it work?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: What is EmSella Therapy, and how does it work?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: What is EmSella Therapy, and how does it work?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-1" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="What is EmSella Therapy, and how does it work?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-1" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">What is EmSella Therapy, and how does it work?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-1" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-1" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>This pelvic floor strengthening chair is a non-invasive treatment designed to strengthen the pelvic floor muscles, which support the bladder and help control urination. At Casa Privée, we use the FDA-approved BTL EMSELLA Chair, also known as the “Kegel Throne.” During a session, you sit comfortably on the chair while it emits electromagnetic energy, causing thousands of muscle contractions in the pelvic area. These contractions are much stronger than those achieved through traditional Kegel exercises, leading to improved muscle tone and better bladder control.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8fah93s-4cece3e8bbedd08cd3ee05dbb08da5e4" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: Who can benefit from Pelvic Floor Therapy?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: Who can benefit from Pelvic Floor Therapy?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: Who can benefit from Pelvic Floor Therapy?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-2" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="Who can benefit from Pelvic Floor Therapy?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-2" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">Who can benefit from Pelvic Floor Therapy?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-2" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-2" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>Our pelvic floor treatments in Miami are suitable for both men and women experiencing urinary incontinence or weakened pelvic floor muscles. This includes individuals dealing with bladder leaks due to aging, childbirth, or other factors. It’s also beneficial for those seeking a non-surgical solution to improve their quality of life without downtime or discomfort.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8fai5qz-97f6b3dfb5f28468e5c70d7fe93b1bdf" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: What does an treatment session involve? " class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: What does an treatment session involve? " data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: What does an treatment session involve? " data-fake-id="#toggle-id-3" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="What does an treatment session involve? " data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-3" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">What does an treatment session involve? <span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-3" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-3" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>During a pelvic floor strengthening session at Casa Privée, you’ll remain fully clothed and sit comfortably on the chair for about 30 minutes. The treatment is painless; you may feel a tingling sensation and muscle contractions in your pelvic area, similar to performing Kegel exercises. There’s no downtime, so you can resume your daily activities immediately after the session.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8faijmx-29b56d3ceb7c482079f7eff0a4fd4d25" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand:  How many sessions are needed to see results?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand:  How many sessions are needed to see results?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse:  How many sessions are needed to see results?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-4" data-slide-speed="200" data-title=" How many sessions are needed to see results?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-4" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0"> How many sessions are needed to see results?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-4" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-4" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>A typical treatment plan includes about six sessions, scheduled twice a week. Some patients notice improvements after a single session, with results continuing to enhance over the following weeks. Consistency is key to achieving optimal outcomes.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8fak2kp-fcf7895fe062b61da43d01d45621426c" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand:  Is pelvic floor rehabilitation with EmSella safe?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand:  Is pelvic floor rehabilitation with EmSella safe?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse:  Is pelvic floor rehabilitation with EmSella safe?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-5" data-slide-speed="200" data-title=" Is pelvic floor rehabilitation with EmSella safe?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-5" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0"> Is pelvic floor rehabilitation with EmSella safe?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-5" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-5" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>Yes, this treatment is FDA-approved and considered safe for treating urinary incontinence. Since it’s non-invasive and doesn’t require surgery or medication, the risk of side effects is minimal. However, it’s essential to consult with your physician or our medical team at Casa Privée to ensure the treatment is appropriate for your specific health needs.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m8fal3zx-9bcee759d188491e4c61703e622c98db" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: How does EmSella compare to traditional pelvic floor exercises?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: How does EmSella compare to traditional pelvic floor exercises?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: How does EmSella compare to traditional pelvic floor exercises?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-6" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="How does EmSella compare to traditional pelvic floor exercises?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-6" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">How does EmSella compare to traditional pelvic floor exercises?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-6" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-6" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>While traditional Kegel exercises target pelvic floor muscles, they can be challenging to perform correctly and consistently. Electromagnetic pelvic floor therapy delivers thousands of powerful muscle contractions in a single session, providing a more intensive and effective workout for the pelvic floor muscles. This leads to faster and more noticeable improvements in bladder control and overall pelvic health. Searching for pelvic floor therapy near me? <a href="contact-us.php">Contact us today to learn more</a> about our pelvic floor support treatment options.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
</div></div>
